## 1. Hooks Command Dispatch for Claude Code

**Location:** `/Users/matthiaswenz/Development/entire/worktrees/cli-claude-statusline/cmd/entire/cli/hooks_cmd.go` (lines 28-75)

The hooks dispatcher registers all built-in agents' hook subcommands. Here's how it works:

```go
func newHooksCmd() *cobra.Command {
	cmd := &cobra.Command{
		Use:    "hooks",
		Short:  "Hook handlers",
		Long:   "Commands called by hooks. These are internal and not for direct user use.",
		Hidden: true,
		Args: cobra.ArbitraryArgs,
		RunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {
			if len(args) < 2 {
				return cmd.Help()
			}
			agentName := types.AgentName(args[0])
			hookName := args[1]
			// ... external agent discovery ...
			return executeAgentHook(cmd, agentName, hookName, true)
		},
	}

	// Register built-in agent hooks
	for _, agentName := range agent.List() {
		ag, err := agent.Get(agentName)
		if err != nil {
			continue
		}
		if handler, ok := agent.AsHookSupport(ag); ok {
			cmd.AddCommand(newAgentHooksCmd(agentName, handler))
		}
	}
	return cmd
}
```

**Hook registration for Claude Code:**

**Location:** `/Users/matthiaswenz/Development/entire/worktrees/cli-claude-statusline/cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go` (lines 19-28)

